   "widgets_values": [
    "## Song generation with ACE-Step 1.5 XL SFT (4B) - MIT\n\n**The song flow.** ACE-Step 1.5 XL is the same family as the 8-step turbo that ships as S19, at **4B** and\n**50 steps / cfg 7**, and it is the one that reliably *sings*: on a style that names a clear lead it put\n**124 of 188 lyric words** into the mix where the turbo, on the same text, produced no vocal at all (E13b).\n\n- **the style is the vocal's on/off switch.** `tags` (node 7) both describes the music and decides whether a\n  voice appears at all, so name it and keep it consistent with the lyric: a \"clear, strong, close-mic lead\"\n  request was obeyed, while a \"shouted male lead\" style came back **whispered** (E13).\n- **`lyrics`** empty means instrumental; size it to the duration (~1.5-3 words per second, so 120 s wants\n  250-350 words - E7).\n- **the seed and the duration are each wired to two consumers** (the text encoder and the sampler / the\n  latent), so the graph cannot disagree with itself - the same pattern as `ace-step.json`.\n- **`ModelSamplingAuraFlow` shift 3** sits between the UNet and the sampler, as upstream's template ships it.\n\n**Files (~19 GB, all MIT, `Comfy-Org/ace_step_1.5_ComfyUI_files`):**\n`models/diffusion_models/acestep_v1.5_xl_sft_bf16.safetensors` \u00b7\n`models/text_encoders/qwen_0.6b_ace15.safetensors` + `qwen_4b_ace15.safetensors` \u00b7\n`models/vae/ace_1.5_vae.safetensors`.\n\n**Cost:** ~50 s of sampling per 120 s song once the model is loaded (a cold first run is minutes); the ground\ntruth for a take is a spectrogram plus ASR - see `audio/README.md` traps. It lands at **0.0 dBFS**.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S23** in `HOWTO.md`  \u00b7  Why it is this way: **E13/E13b** in `audio/EXPERIMENTS.md`.*\n"
   ],
   "properties": {},
   "order": 0
  }
